Package: spatialLagGLM
Title: Spatial Lag Regression for Spatial Transcriptomics
Version: 0.99.5
Authors@R: 
    person("Sahal", "Paladan", email = "sahalpaladan@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-0120-128X"))
Description: Tests each gene in spatial transcriptomics data for association
    between a spot's expression and the expression of its neighbours. For every
    gene, a quasi-Poisson generalized linear model is fitted with a
    library-size offset, user-defined design terms from the colData, and the
    spatial lag of the gene's own normalised counts as an additional covariate.
    The lag is a row-normalised, inverse-distance weighted mean over spots
    within a given radius, computed separately for each sample. The
    coefficient, p-value and adjusted p-value of the lag are stored in the
    rowData of the input SpatialExperiment. Weights are computed in C++ with
    RcppArmadillo, and genes are fitted in parallel with BiocParallel. The
    p-values are intended for exploratory use. Plotting functions and a Shiny
    explorer are included.
